---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { path } from '../lib/paths';
---
<Layout title="Research — Yucheng Xing" active="research">
  <header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Research interests</p><h1>Learning through dynamics.</h1><p>My research connects generative modeling, differential equations, and adaptive computation, with applications in computer vision and graph time series.</p></header>
  <div class="research-list">
    <section class="research-section" id="generative">
      <span class="research-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div><h2>Efficient generative AI</h2><p>I investigate how to control the computation used by diffusion models while retaining useful generative structure. My work explores input-adaptive generation, structured diffusion processes, and conditional image restoration.</p><p>Applications include image generation, rain removal, and forecasting wildfire risk over multiple future horizons.</p><ul class="related"><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.15199">Input-Adaptive Generative Dynamics in Diffusion Models</a></li><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.09054">Spectral-Structured Diffusion for Single-Image Rain Removal</a></li><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.07361">N-Tree Diffusion for Long-Horizon Wildfire Risk Forecasting</a></li></ul></div>
      <aside class="research-note"><span class="eyebrow">Current questions</span><p>How much computation does each input need?</p><p>How can the structure of a task inform the generation process?</p></aside>
    </section>
    <section class="research-section" id="adaptive">
      <span class="research-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div><h2>Adaptive neural architectures</h2><p>I study architectures that adjust computation to the input. Puppet-CNN represents convolutional parameters as a continuous dynamical system, generating layer parameters along a learned trajectory.</p><p>This perspective connects compact model storage with flexible, input-adaptive computation.</p><ul class="related"><li><a href={path('publications/#puppet-cnn')}>Puppet-CNN · ECCV 2026</a></li></ul></div>
      <figure class="research-figure"><img src={path('images/puppet-cnn.png')} alt="Puppet-CNN parameter flow and adaptive convolutional architecture" width="320" height="220" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Puppet-CNN: continuous parameter dynamics.</figcaption></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="research-section" id="continuous">
      <span class="research-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div><h2>Continuous-time neural modeling</h2><p>I use neural differential equations to model motion and graph time series in continuous time. These models provide a natural way to work with irregular observations and evolving relationships.</p><p>My work includes hierarchical human pose forecasting, stochastic prediction on graphs, and unsupervised online denoising.</p><ul class="related"><li><a href={path('publications/#hdg-ode')}>HDG-ODE · ICCV 2023</a></li><li><a href={path('publications/#aggdn')}>AGGDN · ICONIP 2023</a></li><li><a href={path('publications/#infinity-net')}>∞-Net · ICONIP 2024</a></li></ul></div>
      <figure class="research-figure"><img src={path('images/hdg-ode.png')} alt="Hierarchical graph ODE framework for human pose forecasting" width="320" height="200" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>HDG-ODE: hierarchical dynamics for human motion.</figcaption></figure>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>.research-note{padding:28px;background:var(--wash);border-left:2px solid var(--accent);align-self:center}.research-note p{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:21px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink)}.research-note p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}@media(max-width:720px){.research-note{grid-column:2;padding:22px}.research-note p{font-size:19px}}</style>
